# See http://help.github.com/ignore-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# API Keys
secrets.json
RangerTrak-secrets.json
# NOTE: /src/index.html was listed here, but the file is tracked - and gitignore rules
# do not apply to tracked files, so the entry was inert and gave false protection.
# Angular requires index.html to be tracked; the real rule is simply: no keys in it.

# personnel info
/src/assets/imgs/REW
/src/assets/data/ranger*.json

# NOTE: screenshots and other working captures are deliberately NOT listed here.
# They live outside the repository entirely, next to the planning doc, so there is
# nothing to ignore and nothing to advertise. See DEVELOPING.md, "Screenshots".

# The internal planning/roadmap docs (unremediated security findings, named agency
# contacts, commercial strategy) live outside the repo entirely, in
# ../rangertrak-InternalDocs/ - not relying on a gitignore rule to keep them out of the
# public repo.

# compiled output
/dist
/tmp
/out-tsc

# Generated API docs (`npm run compodoc`). Was tracked - 181 files, 8.2 MB - and went
# stale enough to be a liability: it still described AppModule and LazyModule long after
# both were deleted, and it republished a roster of real names and a key-shaped string
# that had already been removed from src/. Regenerate on demand; don't commit it.
/documentation
# Only exists if Bazel was run
/bazel-out

# dependencies
/node_modules

# Old code
/archived
/non-distributed

#Test and non-project stuff
/junk

